1. DEFINITIONS
"Work" means the software, documentation and other files this
license is attached to. "Licensor" means the copyright holder.
"You" means anyone using the Work under this license.
"Modified File" means a file that contains code from the Work and
has been changed by You, or a file derived from a file of the Work
(for example a port or translation into another language).
"Your Files" means files You wrote that are not Modified Files.
"Distribute" means giving a copy, in source or binary form, to
anyone outside Your own legal entity. Your own legal entity
includes people working for You under Your direction, such as
employees and contractors. Using the Work inside Your own
organization is not distribution.

2. GRANT
The Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive,
perpetual license (subject to Section 10) to use, study, copy,
modify, merge, embed and distribute the Work. Each recipient
receives this license directly from the Licensor.

3. USE IS FREE
You may run the Work for any purpose: personal, educational,
commercial or corporate, including as a hosted service. Using the
Work, including running a modified version, creates no obligation
under this license.

4. DISTRIBUTING UNMODIFIED COPIES
You may distribute unmodified copies, in source or binary form, if
You keep the copyright notice and this license text with them.

5. DISTRIBUTING MODIFIED FILES (the "unshackle" rule)
If You Distribute a Modified File, in source or binary form, then:
 (a) You must mark the file as changed and keep existing notices;
 (b) You must make the complete source of the Modified File
     publicly available, free of charge, under this license, from
     the time of distribution and for as long as You distribute it;
 (c) If You distribute binaries, You must tell recipients where to
     find that source.
 (d) Simple way: publishing the Modified File in a public
     repository, with (a) satisfied and a link to it given with
     any binaries, fulfils (b) and (c). Nothing else is required:
     no registration, no notice to the Licensor, no extra
     paperwork.

6. WHAT THIS LICENSE DOES NOT REQUIRE
 (a) Your Files stay Yours. You may license them however You like,
     including under proprietary terms.
 (b) You may combine the Work, modified or not, with other software
     and distribute the combination, as long as the Work's own
     files remain under this license and Section 5 is followed.
 (c) You may distribute a combined work containing Modified Files
     under the GNU GPL (v2 or later), LGPL or AGPL, provided the
     Modified Files' source remains available as Section 5(b)
     requires.
 (d) Copying a small excerpt (no more than 50 lines in total from
     any one file) into another project does not make that
     project's file a Modified File. Keep a comment crediting the
     source.
 (e) You are not required to share changes You never Distribute.

